< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"status","title":"Renoise status","description":"Whether Kumi's bridge in Renoise is connected: the Renoise and bridge versions, the open song, and whether Renoise is busy (a dialog, a render). With several Renoise instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"discover","title":"Find running Renoise","description":"Every running Renoise with Kumi's bridge: process id, port, resource folder, versions, open song, and whether it answers. Use it when status reports none, or to choose among several.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"read","title":"Read Renoise","description":"Rows of one kind from the open Renoise song, a page at a time: {items, nextCursor?, epoch}. Pass parent (a row's ref) to read what is inside it, such as a track's devices or a device's parameters; pass the previous page's nextCursor as cursor for the next page. Or pass ref alone for the one object it names. Refs hold until the epoch changes. With several Renoise instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Renoise process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Renoise resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["song","track","sequence","pattern","line","automation","instrument","sampl